Subject: [PATCH] stream: release and trim the unused blank RGB canvas

Release the placeholder RGB canvas when neither raw nor H.264 output is
configured, retaining the compressed JPEG for HTTP clients. Recreate the
canvas on the next draw when frametext no longer has valid pixels.

On glibc, also ask malloc_trim(0) to return free heap pages to the system.
After an earlier canvas allocation is freed, glibc can raise its adaptive
mmap threshold. A subsequent placeholder update can then allocate its
canvas from the heap, where free() alone may leave its pages resident.
This can outlast a temporary camera startup failure even after capture
recovers. Trimming addresses that allocator retention without changing
sink selection or capture settings. Other C libraries keep free() behavior.

Sink selection remains a runtime check and does not depend on whether
any clients are connected. Raw and H.264 sinks retain their canvas.

Upstream-Status: Pending
